{
 "title": "Geometry nodes 6: rocks, and the finished landscape",
 "summary": "A rock from a cube in geometry nodes: Extrude Mesh on the faces picked by Index + Compare (integer, <= 1), Subdivision Surface, Set Position by a noise texture (Musgrave), smooth, a rock material (two voronoi textures distorted by noise and mixed, a grey ramp, bump); Geometry to Instance, Duplicate Elements (instances), Set Position by Duplicate Index, Rotate and Scale Instances with random vectors: four different rocks. The landscape finished: the library's sand shader copied into a brown soil, denser grass. Beyond the tutorial: the rocks drop onto the hills with a Raycast instead of being placed by hand.",
